course: dictionary
lesson: 10978
title: Warehouses and the clues around them
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A warehouse is a large building where goods are kept before they are sold or sent to shops. You can work this out from the words around it. «In a big warehouse a computer remembers which numbered shelf every box is on.» Big, shelf and box all tell you the warehouse is a place full of stored things.
explain: Look at who works there. «Night shifts mean working through the night and sleeping in the day; nurses, drivers, bakers and warehouse workers often do them.» Warehouse workers are people with jobs, so a warehouse must be a place of work, not just a place to sleep or to play.
explain: The word can also mean a big shop that sells large amounts of goods cheaply. «When Jake was suspended for fighting, the school phoned his dad at the warehouse.» Here the warehouse is his dad's workplace. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: A warehouse is a large building where goods are stored before they are sold or sent to shops.
fact: A warehouse can also be a big shop that sells large amounts of goods cheaply.
fact: «Some warehouses are as big as dozens of football pitches.»
fact: Phrases to remember: warehouse worker, and store in a warehouse.
fact: «Heavy loads go at the bottom so nothing falls.» Warehouse workers stack boxes carefully, with heavy ones low down.
exercise: «A warehouse has 40 shelves with 20 boxes each.» What is a warehouse in this sentence? | A school for robots | A kind of boat for carrying shelves | *A large building for storing boxes | A type of football pitch
exercise: Warehouse workers are people who do what? | Build houses from bricks | Sell ice cream on the beach | Teach lessons in a school | *Work in a building that stores goods
exercise: «Some warehouses are as big as dozens of football pitches.» What does this tell you? | Warehouses are only for toys | Football pitches are used to store goods | *Warehouses can be very large | Warehouses are always small
test: Why might a warehouse use a computer? | *To remember which shelf each box is on | To play music for the workers | To check the weather | To cook the dinner
test: In «Mum bought a sofa at the warehouse, where prices were low», what does warehouse most likely mean? | *A big shop selling goods cheaply | A type of robot | A busy road by the sea | A small room for coats
exam: Which sentence uses warehouse to mean a big store or shop? | *«Mum bought a sofa at the warehouse on the edge of town, where prices were low.» | «The warehouse was covered in snow, and the children built a snowman.» | «The warehouse is a famous painting by a local artist.» | «Warehouse is the name of my favourite song.»
